WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.450
What does federal policy actually require?

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:07.612
Read from the documents, TIC 3.0
is descriptive, not prescriptive.

3
00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:11.430
There are four use cases,
Traditional, Branch Office,

4
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.537
Remote User and Cloud,
and no SASE use case.

5
00:00:14.537 --> 00:00:20.587
The Security Capabilities Catalog,
version 3.3, sets goals, not methods.

6
00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:25.716
Two statements constrain a branch:
policy enforcement parity on every path,

7
00:00:25.716 --> 00:00:30.112
and preserving CISA's visibility
as branches connect directly.

8
00:00:30.112 --> 00:00:38.750
OMB M-26-14 rescinded
M-21-31 on May 22, 2026.

9
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.715
Logs must be searchable for six
months and retrievable for a year,

10
00:00:42.715 --> 00:00:47.488
and must show source and destination
addresses, ports and session attributes.

11
00:00:47.488 --> 00:00:52.487
The first agency logging plan
is due November 18, 2026.

12
00:00:52.487 --> 00:00:57.250
When branches leave MTIPS, the sensor
telemetry CISA received stops.

13
00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.940
The replacement is CLAW, CISA's
Comprehensive Log Aggregation Warehouse,

14
00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:06.025
and onboarding needs the agency,
CISA and the provider together.

15
00:01:06.025 --> 00:01:08.837
Keep MTIPS until CISA confirms parity.

16
00:01:08.837 --> 00:01:11.490
Technology-neutral isn't requirement-free:

17
00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:15.100
four binding obligations still
land on branch equipment.
